# Cloudflare Workers Assets redirects.
# Format: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# The blog moved to roydipta.com/blog/. This deployment exists only to 301 the old
# URLs there, so bookmarks and link equity survive. It must STAY UP: it is the thing
# serving the redirects. Keep it at least a year.
#
# Why every line below is a plain 301 with a literal path:
#
#   - `200` rewrites (`/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200`) are a Cloudflare PAGES
#     feature. On Workers Static Assets they are ignored, and the catch-all then
#     swallowed the URL instead. Verified on production, not assumed.
#   - `:placeholder` rules (`/page/:num`) also lost to the catch-all here, so the
#     two real pagination paths are listed literally.
#   - `wrangler dev` does NOT reproduce production precedence. It passed all of the
#     above locally while production disagreed. Verify redirects against the
#     deployed site, never only against the dev server.
#
# 301 and not 302: only a permanent redirect passes ranking signals.
# Each URL maps to its OWN counterpart: a blanket redirect to one page is read as a
# soft 404, which would throw the signal away.
#
# Matching is case-sensitive and three old URLs carry capitals, so the lowercase
# variants are listed too.

